* ''Plain text survives to disk'' (operator, 2026-11-10: //"The state of play now is 'Dogfood our code into a self-improving AI-Operator alignment harness' so some things must wait. The 'plain text survives to disk' law holds because how do we recover running data between alpha refound otherwise (& this lesson carries forwards, etc)."//). The plaintext projection survives every re-founding by design, so running data recovers across alpha re-foundings (`lares export` and `import`, a reset that keeps `projections/`), and the law carries forward past alpha. Work beyond the truths it needs waits behind the dogfood harness. <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/api/disk-projection#/core-claim`>>.

